radiative-transfer-equation-abf74f4c.conceptual_definition:
The Radiative Transfer Equation is a fundamental equation in astrophysics and other fields that describes how the intensity of radiation changes as it propagates through a medium. It accounts for the processes of emission, absorption, and scattering that affect the radiation field. Specifically, it quantifies the change in specific intensity (
$I_{\nu}$
) along a path (
$s$
) due to emission (
$j_{\nu}$
) and absorption (
$\alpha_{\nu}$
) by the medium.

